cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cameleer in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Cameleer: Apache Camel's integration model in Rust"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sudheesh
    family-names: PM
repository-code: "https://github.com/pmsudhi/cameleer"
url: "https://pmsudhi.github.io/cameleer/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-11-06"
keywords:
  - rust
  - apache-camel
  - enterprise-integration-patterns
  - integration
  - ai-agents
  - serverless
abstract: >-
  Cameleer is an independent reimplementation of Apache Camel in Rust: routes,
  Enterprise Integration Patterns, about 230 components, languages and data formats, and
  the Rust, YAML and XML DSLs, built on the Rust standard library only. In published benchmarks
  with the same routes it starts in 3 ms (Apache Camel on the JVM: 1.1 s), uses up to 54 times less
  memory and handles 1.7 to 8.7 times the throughput.
references:
  - type: software
    title: Apache Camel
    url: "https://camel.apache.org/"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/apache/camel"
    authors:
      - name: The Apache Software Foundation
